                        "review": "Great game and especially so if you ever played the old analogue version of Space Hulk and wanted  something similar. \n\nIt has its faults but if you overcome them its a great little treasure of a game to keep on the back burner, and play a few maps every now and then. \n\nPro's\n-pure nostagia and very much in keeping with the old tabletop game.\n- oldschool 40k vibe \n-A lot of content and the ability to redo missions with your chosen Chapter. \n-Looks pretty good for when it was released.\n\nCons\n\n-some bugs\n-terrible lighting, have to turn the gamma right up, I understand what they were going for but I don't want to develop a squint for the sake of 'immersion'.\n-the difficulty is good, I love it and its very similar to the old game where you are facing down an unceasing horde of enemies. Some players may find that too difficult. \n\n",
